WEBVTT

00:07.270 --> 00:12.820
The Faraway Paladin

00:09.110 --> 00:12.820
<b><u>The Lord of the Rust Mountains</u></b>

01:30.190 --> 01:37.780
The Messenger in the Burial Chamber

01:30.830 --> 01:32.880
Has it really been two years,

01:32.880 --> 01:34.740
warrior of the light?

01:35.100 --> 01:36.420
Stagnate...

01:36.420 --> 01:37.960
The god of the undead?

01:38.940 --> 01:40.750
Defending isn't an option here.

01:41.120 --> 01:41.870
We have to—

01:41.870 --> 01:43.590
Now, wait just a minute.

01:43.590 --> 01:46.320
If you intend to fight, you two will win.

01:46.320 --> 01:49.560
I'm not an Echo today, after all.

01:51.570 --> 01:52.620
A Herald?

01:53.110 --> 01:55.080
Very astute.

01:55.080 --> 01:58.080
Thanks to the utter thrashing 
you gave me last time,

01:58.080 --> 02:02.600
it's unlikely I'll be able to send 
an Echo to this world for a while,

02:02.600 --> 02:04.640
no matter how hard I try.

02:04.870 --> 02:05.960
<i>Heralds...</i>

02:06.340 --> 02:08.650
<i>Messengers of the gods 
that convey their will.</i>

02:08.940 --> 02:11.610
I had no choice but to send a Herald...

02:11.610 --> 02:13.140
Enjoying a little fishing?

02:13.140 --> 02:15.410
Again, very astute.

02:15.410 --> 02:18.390
You are as sharp as ever, I see.

02:18.660 --> 02:22.430
<i>They knew if they tossed enough bait 
for the undead around here,</i>

02:22.430 --> 02:24.730
<i>there was a good chance I'd bite.</i>

02:25.610 --> 02:26.910
That's despicable.

02:27.180 --> 02:31.650
Regular fishing is despicable, too, 
from the fish's point of view.

02:31.650 --> 02:34.220
But that's just how gods are.

02:35.470 --> 02:40.320
You don't appear to be seeking 
revenge for last time.

02:40.790 --> 02:42.740
First, let me apologize.

02:42.740 --> 02:44.100
Apologize?

02:44.100 --> 02:48.250
The Echo you faced last time behaved 
shamefully in its dying moments.

02:48.250 --> 02:50.800
For that, I am deeply ashamed.

02:51.060 --> 02:58.210
Newborn Echos tend to be very emotional, 
rash, and generally infantile.

02:58.210 --> 03:00.510
Still, that is no excuse.

03:00.510 --> 03:03.650
Th-The god of the undead is apologizing?

03:03.650 --> 03:09.790
Young dwarf, that strong warrior 
you're with killed me.

03:09.790 --> 03:11.950
All that stabbing and being stabbed...

03:11.950 --> 03:14.230
What a fiery night that was.

03:14.230 --> 03:17.230
I wasn't aware that gods 
had a fondness for jokes.

03:17.670 --> 03:19.600
Just tell me what it is you want.

03:19.600 --> 03:21.420
Oh, you're no fun.

03:21.420 --> 03:24.960
Would it kill you to humor 
me while I chat a little?

03:25.310 --> 03:29.480
<i>This god can speak the Words. 
That's what makes them so dangerous.</i>

03:29.790 --> 03:34.310
Brave warrior who defeated me, 
Paladin of the Light...

03:34.310 --> 03:36.820
This is my revelation.

03:42.840 --> 03:44.150
Sir Will!

03:44.500 --> 03:49.160
William, armed with the blessing of 
light, you will face the dragon...

03:49.160 --> 03:52.050
and you will die in defeat.

03:54.360 --> 03:56.390
If you do not wish to die in vain,

03:56.390 --> 04:00.420
do not fight the Gods' Sickle, 
the evil dragon Valacirca.

04:00.940 --> 04:02.580
If you do not believe me,

04:02.580 --> 04:05.860
feel free to ask the goddess Gracefeel.

04:06.570 --> 04:08.860
Why are you telling me this?

04:09.650 --> 04:13.460
Because you proved that you have 
what it takes to be a hero.

04:13.460 --> 04:16.190
I love humans,

04:16.190 --> 04:18.830
and I am especially partial to heroes.

04:19.190 --> 04:23.570
I find the radiance of their 
souls to be truly beautiful.

04:23.880 --> 04:27.100
That is exactly why I desire 
undeath and eternity for them.

04:27.510 --> 04:30.790
I cannot bear to see souls dragged 
down by the fools of this world

04:30.790 --> 04:33.590
so that they lose their radiance 
among bitterness and regret,

04:33.590 --> 04:39.600
and I would hate to see you killed by the 
likes of a vulgar beast like Valacirca.

04:39.600 --> 04:40.580
Vulgar?

04:40.830 --> 04:45.250
In the age of myth, when I was 
still on the side of good,

04:45.250 --> 04:47.210
I met him once—

04:47.640 --> 04:51.370
the Gods' Sickle, the evil dragon Valacirca.

04:51.370 --> 04:53.730
He fought not for any beliefs,

04:53.730 --> 04:56.720
but for the sake of victory and plunder.

04:57.220 --> 05:00.620
I'm surprised the virtuous 
gods employed him.

05:00.890 --> 05:05.420
If a mercenary is not on your side, 
he will end up on your enemy's side.

05:05.820 --> 05:10.620
After that, I betrayed the virtuous 
gods for the sake of my beliefs.

05:10.620 --> 05:12.610
Many battles were fought,

05:12.610 --> 05:16.240
and many of the old gods left this world.

05:16.900 --> 05:19.540
<i>It's the same myth Gus told me.</i>

05:19.540 --> 05:21.490
But he was different.

05:21.490 --> 05:22.860
Do you mean...

05:22.860 --> 05:26.370
he is a remnant of the age of the gods?

05:26.710 --> 05:30.740
Precisely. And he remained a mercenary...

05:30.740 --> 05:34.810
including during the great uprising 
led by the demons from the abyss.

05:36.450 --> 05:38.630
The Great Cataclysm of 
two hundred years ago...

05:39.020 --> 05:40.900
The end of the Union Age.

05:41.210 --> 05:43.940
He was hired by the demon army,

05:43.940 --> 05:46.090
caused the fall of the Rust Mountains,

05:46.090 --> 05:47.570
and then fell asleep.

05:48.110 --> 05:50.610
His battle wounds were too severe.

05:50.910 --> 05:52.560
W-Wait a moment!

05:52.560 --> 05:56.260
Did you say "battle wounds"? My ancestors...

05:56.260 --> 06:00.340
Ah, of course. You are a survivor 
of the mountain people?

06:00.340 --> 06:01.410
Y-Yes.

06:03.940 --> 06:07.800
Well, well! Perhaps there really 
is such a thing as fate!

06:08.220 --> 06:09.790
Very well, then.

06:09.790 --> 06:12.390
Descendant of the Iron Country,

06:12.390 --> 06:16.430
I, Stagnate, God of Undead, 
shall tell you the truth:

06:16.780 --> 06:22.440
that the king of the Iron Mountains, 
Aurvangr, was a true hero!

06:23.060 --> 06:24.310
You should be proud.

06:24.310 --> 06:27.520
The famed sword handed down through 
the generations, Calldawn,

06:27.520 --> 06:31.150
took an eye from the evil dragon 
that survives from the age of gods!

06:31.150 --> 06:33.450
I-Is that true?

06:33.450 --> 06:37.580
How exhilarating it was! 
He was truly a great hero!

06:40.840 --> 06:42.180
I'm so glad...

06:42.550 --> 06:43.860
I'm so glad...

06:45.650 --> 06:48.520
<i>I wouldn't have expected such 
kindness from an evil god.</i>

06:48.520 --> 06:52.930
<i>But this is a god who distorts the rules 
of life and death and brings disaster</i>

06:52.930 --> 06:54.790
<i>because their emotions lead them to.</i>

06:54.790 --> 06:55.960
William...

06:56.480 --> 07:00.410
In time, you may surpass even 
Aurvangr's great achievements

07:00.410 --> 07:02.980
and succeed in slaying Valacirca.

07:02.980 --> 07:06.330
But now is not that time.

07:12.520 --> 07:15.070
The dragon's sleep grows shallow.

07:16.980 --> 07:20.110
The dragon has just given 
us a show of his power.

07:20.630 --> 07:24.320
Go home at once. Chaos is imminent.

07:42.890 --> 07:43.860
Ru!

07:51.630 --> 07:54.360
This is the cry of the dragon...

07:54.900 --> 07:57.420
The Dragon Roar.

08:01.590 --> 08:06.320
<i>The overwhelming might of a ruler, 
striking fear into all living things...</i>

08:12.730 --> 08:15.510
Something troublesome is 
coming along with it.

08:15.510 --> 08:18.420
Even you will likely 
struggle a bit with this.

08:30.740 --> 08:32.490
A g-giant?!

08:32.490 --> 08:34.120
That's a forest giant!

08:34.120 --> 08:36.450
They're normally a mild-mannered race!

08:37.360 --> 08:41.140
He's been hit by the Dragon Roar. 
He is not in his right mind.

08:41.670 --> 08:43.910
What will you do? Kill him?

08:44.450 --> 08:45.450
Of course not.

08:45.970 --> 08:48.920
The brute force that well-trained 
muscles give you

08:48.920 --> 08:51.460
can solve most problems, you know!

08:51.690 --> 08:52.850
Sir Will!

08:58.270 --> 08:59.800
This is nothing!

09:08.860 --> 09:11.430
H-He just...

09:11.430 --> 09:13.600
...flung a giant, yes.

09:14.700 --> 09:17.760
Shine the light of reason 
upon the fog of confusion.

09:21.980 --> 09:25.120
I'm awful sorry about that.

09:25.120 --> 09:26.320
Can you make it home?

09:26.320 --> 09:27.740
I think so.

09:27.880 --> 09:31.000
<b>I speak... giant language...</b>

09:32.130 --> 09:32.760
<b>little bit.</b>

09:33.260 --> 09:35.630
<b>You do? Well, that's great!</b>

09:36.400 --> 09:37.630
Uh...

09:37.630 --> 09:41.010
<b>Dragon... roaring... dangerous.</b>

09:41.360 --> 09:44.140
Yeah, it sure is scary, but...

09:44.140 --> 09:47.270
<b>I must return to my clan.</b>

09:47.650 --> 09:51.730
<b>I will move to a safer place after that.</b>

09:55.530 --> 09:58.030
I am Gangr of the Jotunn.

09:58.030 --> 10:01.910
<b>William, hero of man, I will never forget this debt.</b>

10:07.960 --> 10:11.190
This is the first time 
I've ever seen a giant.

10:11.190 --> 10:12.380
Me, too.

10:12.380 --> 10:14.310
Yet you can speak their language?

10:14.310 --> 10:17.880
My magic teacher had immense 
knowledge and an amazing memory.

10:18.250 --> 10:19.650
You saw it.

10:20.500 --> 10:24.110
That is the power of the ancient 
dragon that even the demons fear.

10:24.110 --> 10:27.190
Should he awaken and seek another uprising,

10:27.190 --> 10:31.700
you will have no choice but to defeat 
him, but you won't be enough.

10:32.010 --> 10:34.480
So I'm supposed to accept 
sacrifices for the cause?

10:34.480 --> 10:38.240
Even if you're my enemy, that doesn't 
seem like something you'd say.

10:38.240 --> 10:41.470
A thousand lives cannot take 
the place of ten thousand.

10:41.470 --> 10:43.450
As infuriating as it is,

10:43.450 --> 10:48.270
so long as you live, more people can 
be saved, so there is no choice.

10:48.720 --> 10:51.030
Think long and hard on it,

10:51.030 --> 10:54.740
bringer of the light... the Faraway Paladin.

10:55.580 --> 10:59.190
Farewell. We will meet again.

10:59.960 --> 11:02.490
They seem partial to you.

11:02.490 --> 11:04.600
They had their eye on me, that's all.

11:04.600 --> 11:07.590
They say the gods wish for heroes.

11:07.860 --> 11:12.020
That they send proxies to the living 
world to make their divine will known.

11:12.020 --> 11:16.480
You are the hero who symbolizes the 
goddess of light. Is that why...

11:16.760 --> 11:19.640
The god of undead wants me 
to feel indebted to them.

11:20.350 --> 11:23.490
What do you plan to do from here?

11:24.130 --> 11:25.360
Good question...

11:26.660 --> 11:28.730
I wonder what I should do...

11:30.500 --> 11:35.630
<i>The Dragon Roar caused great 
damage throughout Beast Woods.</i>

11:35.970 --> 11:38.340
<i>In order to take in people 
who lost their homes,</i>

11:38.340 --> 11:39.870
<i>treat the injured,</i>

11:40.300 --> 11:42.680
<i>and subjugate the demons 
now running rampant,</i>

11:42.680 --> 11:45.130
<i>I sent out adventurers all over the place.</i>

11:45.610 --> 11:48.900
<i>If the dragon were to awaken 
and fly this way on a whim,</i>

11:49.300 --> 11:53.490
<i>it would destroy not only Torch Port, 
but likely Whitesails, as well.</i>

11:54.280 --> 11:55.990
<i>There's no doubt about it.</i>

11:55.990 --> 11:59.180
<i>The evil dragon is accompanied 
by high-ranking demons.</i>

11:59.180 --> 12:02.290
<i>I sincerely doubt you can 
defeat them on your own.</i>

12:02.960 --> 12:04.260
<i>Of course...</i>

12:06.700 --> 12:09.430
<i>There's nothing shameful about running away.</i>

12:11.880 --> 12:17.220
You said that under the assumption that 
I'd be the one going, right, Bishop?

12:22.010 --> 12:23.290
<i>Goddess...</i>

12:24.380 --> 12:28.030
<i>If you would only tell me that 
there's a way for me to win,</i>

12:28.600 --> 12:31.440
<i>or if you told me to fight, 
even if I couldn't win...</i>

12:31.440 --> 12:35.490
<i>If you ordered me to prove my 
righteousness, I'm sure I...</i>

12:36.610 --> 12:40.420
<i>Back when I couldn't move forward, 
when I was mired in frustration,</i>

12:40.420 --> 12:43.110
<i>when time was just passing 
me by as I sat idle...</i>

12:44.020 --> 12:47.680
<i>I was reborn, raised with love,</i>

12:47.680 --> 12:49.920
<i>respected and acknowledged,</i>

12:49.920 --> 12:52.200
<i>and regarded as the central 
figure among my peers.</i>

12:56.940 --> 12:57.920
I'm coming in.

13:02.020 --> 13:03.900
Wrestling with yourself again?

13:04.500 --> 13:05.290
Yeah.

13:06.510 --> 13:08.720
So that's why you didn't notice.

13:08.720 --> 13:11.860
Look outside. We've got a bit of trouble.

13:11.860 --> 13:12.520
Huh?

13:18.150 --> 13:20.560
We want to know your intentions, paladin!

13:20.880 --> 13:23.630
Are you going to slay the dragon?

13:23.940 --> 13:26.640
What is the purpose of asking him that?!

13:26.640 --> 13:29.910
Failure to slay the dragon is a 
sin that falls upon us dwarfs!

13:29.910 --> 13:33.410
If you intend to slay it, 
let us accompany you!

13:33.410 --> 13:35.900
Stop this! The dragon is a formidable foe!

13:35.900 --> 13:39.370
The paladin is trying 
to come up with a plan!

13:39.370 --> 13:41.860
I don't know what he's ordered you to do,

13:41.860 --> 13:44.190
but stop trying to buy him time!

13:44.190 --> 13:46.210
He hasn't ordered me to do anything!

13:46.210 --> 13:48.460
I'm telling all of you not to panic!

13:48.460 --> 13:50.120
Did you say "panic"?!

13:50.120 --> 13:54.700
Even if we all banded together, we couldn't 
even leave a mark on the dragon!

13:55.630 --> 13:57.480
I'm going in there!

13:57.970 --> 14:00.530
I'm telling you to stop!

14:04.690 --> 14:09.630
You... All of you are too 
old to even defeat me now!

14:09.630 --> 14:12.190
I don't want to see you all die in vain!

14:12.190 --> 14:13.460
Young Master.

14:14.550 --> 14:16.060
Grendir...

14:16.060 --> 14:18.640
You have grown well.

14:19.060 --> 14:26.310
However... However, that is 
precisely why I... why we...

14:27.090 --> 14:30.350
wish to die.

14:31.480 --> 14:36.680
We wanted to die by our king's side.

14:39.080 --> 14:42.430
But we were not permitted to. 
We had to abandon our pride.

14:42.430 --> 14:47.470
These two hundred years of miserable 
wandering have been so long.

14:47.470 --> 14:52.560
Surely that is enough. 
We have done more than our share.

14:52.560 --> 14:55.860
We have persisted in 
believing that, and now...

14:55.860 --> 15:00.070
At long last, we have learned 
that the loathsome dragon lives!

15:00.380 --> 15:02.100
What is so wrong with wishing

15:02.100 --> 15:06.010
for the continuation of that day, 
that we may die fighting?!

15:06.350 --> 15:10.260
Let me through! I will ask the 
paladin what he intends to do!

15:10.550 --> 15:11.800
I will not!

15:12.300 --> 15:13.800
Grendir!

15:27.350 --> 15:31.100
You ask what's so wrong 
with that wish, Grendir?

15:31.750 --> 15:34.600
All of you are already so fixated on dying

15:34.600 --> 15:36.850
that you aren't even thinking of winning.

15:37.450 --> 15:39.030
And that won't do.

15:39.590 --> 15:41.460
You know that won't do.

15:42.010 --> 15:45.860
The proud warriors of the mountain 
only throw down their lives

15:45.860 --> 15:47.650
for the sake of victory!

15:48.220 --> 15:51.000
It was all of you who taught me that!

15:51.320 --> 15:52.290
Young Master...

15:52.290 --> 15:53.190
Young Master...

15:53.190 --> 15:54.000
Young Master...

15:54.490 --> 15:58.760
I promise you that the paladin 
will make his decision!

15:58.760 --> 16:01.420
And when he does, I will 
be there by his side

16:01.420 --> 16:04.270
to win back the dwarfs' honor!

16:05.070 --> 16:10.020
I swear on the name of Aurvangr, 
the last king of the Iron Country!

16:10.020 --> 16:13.430
As his grandson, I, Vindalfr,

16:13.430 --> 16:16.780
will take back the mountains 
that belonged to my ancestors!

16:19.200 --> 16:21.850
He's pretty valiant, huh?

16:22.170 --> 16:23.260
Yeah.

16:23.260 --> 16:25.010
He can't afford to lose.

16:25.010 --> 16:25.740
Yeah.

16:26.380 --> 16:30.290
You usually never think about pros and cons

16:30.290 --> 16:33.420
or whether or not you can 
actually win, do you?

16:35.540 --> 16:37.680
So that's how you should be now, too.

16:49.380 --> 16:50.890
I will slay the dragon.

16:52.970 --> 16:55.400
I've made up my mind to slay the dragon.

16:55.400 --> 16:57.840
Ru... Vindalfr.

16:57.840 --> 17:00.620
I commend your proclamation that you'll 
reclaim your ancestors' mountains.

17:01.310 --> 17:02.830
Will you accompany me?

17:03.670 --> 17:07.020
I had faith that you would ask me to!

17:07.020 --> 17:08.160
With pleasure!

17:08.160 --> 17:10.690
You sure you want to agree that quickly?

17:10.690 --> 17:15.350
You ask that, but I know you had every 
intention of following him yourself.

17:15.350 --> 17:17.630
Hey, you've grown a spine, I see.

17:18.410 --> 17:22.060
We're up against a dragon. 
Numbers won't help.

17:22.520 --> 17:25.180
We can't spare a lot of the 
city's defenses, either.

17:25.180 --> 17:28.140
So there's me, you, and Will,

17:28.140 --> 17:31.570
and we'll need a guide who knew 
the mountains 200 years ago.

17:31.820 --> 17:32.710
I will—

17:32.710 --> 17:34.770
No, I will go.

17:35.280 --> 17:37.820
This is no job for a man who wants to die.

17:37.820 --> 17:42.080
Besides, you have an obligation 
to keep our people united.

17:42.830 --> 17:44.750
I shall be your guide.

17:45.160 --> 17:48.480
Ghelreis! I appreciate it!

17:49.430 --> 17:51.220
And then there's me.

17:51.920 --> 17:53.450
Reystov?

17:53.450 --> 17:57.060
I came to see what the 
big crowd was all about.

17:57.350 --> 17:59.570
You're as sharp as ever.

17:59.570 --> 18:03.800
So we're five men picking a fight 
with demons and an evil dragon.

18:04.660 --> 18:06.310
Do we have a chance?

18:06.310 --> 18:07.200
No.

18:08.320 --> 18:11.290
There's no surefire method 
for killing a dragon.

18:12.070 --> 18:13.990
We'll be at a disadvantage.

18:13.990 --> 18:15.980
Will you still accompany me?

18:16.590 --> 18:17.350
Yes!

18:17.830 --> 18:20.200
That's exactly where glory and honor lie.

18:20.200 --> 18:22.330
That is a warrior's true worth.

18:22.560 --> 18:25.840
I'm used to having to go 
along with your crazy ideas.

18:26.210 --> 18:30.050
Let's go slay a dragon and 
take back the mountains!

18:36.250 --> 18:37.750
So you're going?

18:40.440 --> 18:41.410
Yeah.

18:41.410 --> 18:44.070
Please... Please, be safe.

18:51.180 --> 18:53.690
I'm here!

18:53.690 --> 18:54.900
Bee!

18:55.420 --> 18:57.230
You're going to slay a dragon, right?

18:57.230 --> 18:58.120
Yeah.

18:58.120 --> 19:02.440
Then I can write a song about it, 
like I promised, right?

19:02.440 --> 19:03.840
Of course!

19:04.880 --> 19:07.840
I get to write a new dragon-slaying saga!

19:07.840 --> 19:09.950
It's a troubadour's dream!

19:10.970 --> 19:13.450
I'll start by spreading 
the prequel far and wide.

19:13.450 --> 19:14.800
You need that, right?

19:14.800 --> 19:18.340
Yeah, definitely. Thank you.

19:18.340 --> 19:20.990
But don't give me a sad ending, you hear?

19:20.990 --> 19:23.070
I'll try my best not to.

19:23.070 --> 19:27.300
Yes, do that! Nobody likes 
tragic twists anymore!

19:31.410 --> 19:33.440
Please don't leave me behind...

19:34.440 --> 19:35.860
Sorry about that!

19:36.560 --> 19:40.370
I've secured the supplies 
I figured you would need.

19:40.370 --> 19:43.210
You determined so quickly that I'd be going?

19:43.210 --> 19:48.020
Yes, and I was still anxious that I 
might not reach you before you left.

19:48.020 --> 19:49.910
I was just hesitating for a while.

19:49.910 --> 19:53.220
I'll write in your song that you were 
just waiting for the right time!

19:53.220 --> 19:55.080
That sounds cooler, right?

19:55.080 --> 19:56.990
You exaggerating like that is

19:56.990 --> 20:01.080
what makes Sir William look more and 
more like some incredible strategist!

20:02.800 --> 20:05.740
I hesitate just like anyone else.

20:05.740 --> 20:08.220
I don't want to die, and I don't like pain.

20:08.220 --> 20:09.730
But you're still going, right?

20:09.730 --> 20:10.520
Yes.

20:11.080 --> 20:13.850
The vow I made to the goddess 
was just that important.

20:13.850 --> 20:17.290
I'll be using that line in 
my song, just so you know!

20:17.640 --> 20:21.730
Pious warrior, devoted to his 
goddess, and hero of the light!

20:21.730 --> 20:25.110
May the wind of fortune 
be ever at your back!

20:26.170 --> 20:29.930
Will, I won't tell you not to 
be reckless or try too hard.

20:29.930 --> 20:32.360
I know now is the time 
when this must be done.

20:32.360 --> 20:35.760
If there are any other supplies 
you need, please let me know.

20:37.060 --> 20:41.300
In that case, there's one big 
thing I'd like to ask for...

20:56.730 --> 20:58.120
You are going, then?

21:00.370 --> 21:03.280
I do not wish to see you die.

21:03.570 --> 21:06.810
I am honored. Thank you.

21:06.810 --> 21:09.080
You still insist on going?

21:09.080 --> 21:12.030
In order to keep your promise to me?

21:12.030 --> 21:12.780
Yes.

21:13.320 --> 21:17.050
Then I cannot say your 
decision defies my will.

21:17.620 --> 21:21.500
That promise is shared by 
the two of us, after all.

21:22.270 --> 21:23.960
Kneel.

21:30.880 --> 21:33.690
I command you, William...

21:34.790 --> 21:38.640
Do not fear. I am with you at all times.

21:39.040 --> 21:41.480
I am your goddess.

21:41.480 --> 21:46.570
I will strengthen you, 
aid you, and protect you.

21:46.570 --> 21:50.910
Go. Slay the dragon, 
and fulfill your promise,

21:50.910 --> 21:52.610
my knight.

21:58.720 --> 22:00.340
On your light.

23:35.640 --> 23:39.980
A Brief Return Home
